      "punte": [
        "fix: [taal] in 'Kennis wat vroeër dae geneem het om te vind': 'Kennis wat vroeër dae geneem het om te vind' copies English, and 'vroeër dae' reads at first as the idiom 'in the old days', so the reader stumbles.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Hospitale, banke en winkels werk elke dag hiermee. / Skole en laborato': The first five items are 'Om ...' phrases that answer the heading; the last two are full sentences about who uses computers, so the list is not parallel. Fixing it needs a content choice, so it is left to the writer.",
        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Ons noem dit 'n wêreldwye netwerk van rekenaars wat inligting met meka': The study text calls the internet a network of computers, while the glossary entry calls it a network of networks; not a language fault, but a reader comparing the two gets two descriptions."
      ]
